Description: transparent proxy that captures LoRaWAN gateway traffic
 Sits between LoRaWAN gateways and a network server, decoding every uplink
 and downlink in real time, and can block selected messages. It speaks the
 Semtech UDP packet forwarder protocol and ChirpStack Concentratord, stores
 what it sees in a SQLite database and serves a web interface and an HTTP
 API from the same program.
 .
 The program is one static binary with no dependencies on other packages. It
 runs as a sandboxed systemd service and is configured in
 /etc/lorawan-sniffer/sniffer.toml.
